    "title": "How to watch Warriors vs Clippers Play-In game without cable tonight",
    "text": "The Warriors face the Clippers in a win-or-go-home Play-In game with their season on the lineBilly CaddenThe Warriors’ season comes down to this. After a year filled with injuries and inconsistency, Golden State finished 37-45 and secured the No. 10 seed in the Western Conference, keeping their playoff hopes alive through the Play-In Tournament. Tonight, they face the Clippers in a win-or-go-home showdown. Lose, and the season is over. Win, and they’ll move on to face the Suns for a shot at the No. 8 seed and a first-round matchup against the Thunder. Steph Curry is back after missing a significant portion of the season with a knee injury, and his presence gives the Dubs a fighting chance, even without Jimmy Butler and Moses Moody, who are both out for the year.For Warriors fans, this game carries even more weight. With Curry nearing the later stages of his career, there’s a real sense that opportunities like this may not come around forever. On the other side, the Clippers bring a fully healthy Kawhi Leonard, who’s been playing at an elite level reminiscent of his championship run in 2019. These teams just met in the regular season finale, with LA taking a 115-110 win even without Kawhi, so Golden State is up against it. The Warriors enter as 5.5-point underdogs, but with Curry on the floor, all it takes is a few timely threes to flip the script. This is one Warriors fans won’t want to miss.The Warriors vs Clippers Play-In game tips off tonight at 7:00 p.m. PDT, and fans across the country can watch it exclusively on Prime Video.When is Warriors vs Clippers? What: Golden State Warriors @ Los Angeles Clippers — Play-In Tournament Game When: Wednesday, April 15, 2026, at 7:00 p.m. PDT Where: Intuit Dome, Inglewood, CA TV: Prime Video How to stream the Warriors vs Clippers game Play-In cableUnlike most of the NBA playoff games coming soon, the entire Play-In tournament, including tonight’s Warriors vs Clippers game, will be streamed exclusively on Amazon Prime Video. This means you won’t be able to tune in on cable TV, NBC Sports Bay Area, or any streaming platform. Instead, you’ll need to sign up for Amazon Prime.If the Warriors win tonight, you’ll need Prime Video to tune into their next Play-In game, so now’s the perfect time to sign up. In addition to just the six Play-In games, Prime is set to air roughly one-third of the first and second round playoff games this postseason, so it’s basically a must-have for NBA fans at this point. Note that all games being aired on Prime are exclusive to the platform, so if you want to watch as many playoff games as possible, you’ll need to be a member.While there are certainly better streaming services than Prime in a vacuum, it’s important to remember that this is only one small part of what the membership offers. Most people who sign up for Amazon Prime do it for the shopping benefits first and foremost, and the streaming platform is seen as a nice little bonus. As a Prime member, in addition to watching these NBA games, you’ll unlock: Free delivery on many Amazon purchases Free GrubHub+ membership Amazon key for safer, in-garage delivery Prime Day and Prime-member exclusive deals Amazon music unlimited …and more. So while it might be frustrating to have to sign up for yet another streaming service to watch tonight’s game and a bunch of NBA playoff games, a Prime membership gets you a heck of a lot more than just digital entertainment. And at just $14.99/month, it remains arguably one of the best overall values for subscriptions. So sign up today and watch the Warriors take on the Clippers tonight.April 15, 2026Andrew Koopman is a freelance writer who's been producing content since 2020. If he's not writing, Andrew is almost certainly watching sports (go Warriors!) or planning his next adventure as he attempts to visit all 50 states in the next few years.",
